{"name":"Fire Dragon Bright","hex":"#f97306","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (usually self-sustaining) chemical reaction involving the bonding of oxygen with carbon or other fuel, with the production of heat and the presence of flame or smouldering.","An instance of this chemical reaction, especially when intentionally created and maintained in a specific location to a useful end (such as a campfire or a hearth fire)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Amazing; excellent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire"},{"term":"dragon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical reptilian or serpentine creature.","In European mythologies, a gigantic beast, typically reptilian with leathery bat-like wings, lion-like claws, scaly skin and a lizard-like body, often a monster with fiery breath."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of drag queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragon"},{"term":"bright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Emitting much light; visually dazzling; luminous, lucent, radiant.","Of light: brilliant, intense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brightness, glow.\n\n Glory, splendour.","Brightness, glow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fire Dragon","blocks":[{"text":"Fire Dragon (火雲傳奇) is a 1994 Hong Kong wuxia film directed by Yuen Woo-ping, starring Brigitte Lin as the eponymous protagonist."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/Fire_Dragon_DVD_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_Dragon"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire"},{"title":"Dragon","blocks":[{"text":"A dragon is a mythical creature found in the folklore of cultures throughout the world. It is roughly serpentine in form, and often possesses features drawn from different animals, such as wings and claws. In nearly all cultures, it is conceived of as a powerful and awe-inspiring creature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png/330px-St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif/500px-Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif/500px-Potjiekos_over_a_fire.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Food being cooked in a cauldron above fire in South Africa.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APotjiekos_over_a_fire.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/The_Great_Fire_of_London%2C_with_Ludg